## ***********************************************************************
## **
## **  SHIM.FUTILBANK.INC.BL -- the low memory front door to the banked FILE
## **  modules, FILEDIR and FILEIO. Both run in SHIM.FUTILBANK, which this file
## **  owns. The FD in the name was FILEDIR's alone until FILEIO joined it.
## **
## **      FILE.DIR.INIT   FILE.DIR.OPEN   FILE.DIR.NEXT
## **      FILE.STATUS     FILE.EXISTS     FILE.DELETE     FILE.RENAME
## **      FILE.MKDIR      FILE.RMDIR      FILE.CHDIR      FILE.UP
## **      FILE.CURDIR     FILE.SAVEARRAY  FILE.LOADARRAY  FILE.SIZE
## **
## **  Shims of exactly the kind SHIM.GUIBANK.INC.BL holds, and they are in a file
## **  of their own for one reason: BASLOAD resolves every label in every file
## **  it reads, so a shim naming FILE.DIR.OPEN.BODY stops the build with
## **  LABEL NOT FOUND in any program that does not also include FILEDIR.
## **  They lived in SHIM.GUIBANK for a day and PICKDEMO -- which banks the same six
## **  modules and has no use for a directory reader -- could not be tokenised
## **  at all. THE SAME NOW GOES FOR FILEIO: include this file and you must
## **  include both modules, or the FILE.RMDIR.BODY shim below fails the same
## **  way. Split this file in two the day a program wants only one of them.
## **
## **  #IFDEF cannot answer it either: SHIM.GUIBANK's whole body is already inside
## **  an #IFNDEF and BASLOAD does not nest them.
## **
## **  THE FILE MODULES GET A REGION OF THEIR OWN. FILEDIR shared SHIM.GUIBANK
## **  with the GUI until 2026-09-09 and was moved out to make room: bank 4 was
## **  at 7,424 of its 8,192 bytes with FILEDIR still in it, and GUI.FORM has
## **  to fit. FILEIO followed it out of SHIM.UTILBANK the same day, which frees
## **  no low RAM -- it was already banked -- but puts the two file modules in
## **  one bank and hands their bytes back to bank 7 for whatever has to leave
## **  the GUI's next.
## **
## **  THE SHIMS PUT THE CALLER'S BANK BACK. FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH keeps it and
## **  FUTIL.SHIM.POP restores it, so a call through here returns with whatever
## **  bank the caller had selected, and a caller inside ANOTHER region may use
## **  these front doors. SHIM.UTILBANK.INC.BL's header holds the full account
## **  of why it is a stack, why POP is reached by GOTO and why the capture has
## **  to be a blob; this file's copy is the same code under its own names.
## **
## **  A REGION MAY NOT REACH INTO ANOTHER REGION DIRECTLY. Every region lives
## **  at $A000, so a GOSUB to FILE.DIR.OPEN.BODY from outside this bank lands
## **  on whatever the caller's bank holds at that address. The front doors
## **  below are the only way in, and they are in low memory, which is what
## **  lets them hold the BANK a region may not contain.
## **
## **  FILEDIR READS FILEIO'S FILE.CHAN, which is a variable and not a call, so
## **  the two were legal in one bank before any of this and still are.
## **
## **  Usage -- each front door sits directly above the region it opens, so a
## **  bank reads as one unit and its file list is the copy list:
## **      GOTO MY.LIBEND
## **      #INCLUDE "SHIM.GUIBANK.INC.BL"
## **      GP.BANKED SHIM.GUIBANK
## **      ...the six GUI modules...
## **      GP.ENDBANKED
## **      #INCLUDE "SHIM.FUTILBANK.INC.BL"
## **      GP.BANKED SHIM.FUTILBANK
## **      #INCLUDE "FILEIO.BANK.INC.BL"        ' FIRST: it supplies FILE.CHAN
## **      #INCLUDE "FILEDIR.BANK.INC.BL"
## **      GP.ENDBANKED
## **      MY.LIBEND:
## **
## **  FILEIO GOES FIRST. It supplies #DEFINE FILE.CHAN and FILEDIR uses it,
## **  and BASLOAD substitutes a #DEFINE where it stands, so the file that
## **  supplies one has to be read before the file that wants it.
## **
## **  Claim the bank as well, or something else will hand it out:
## **      BANKMGR.SET.BANK = SHIM.FUTILBANK : GOSUB BANKMGR.CLAIM
## **
## **  FILE STATEMENTS ARE NOT A REASON to keep a module out of a region: OPEN,
## **  INPUT#, PRINT# and CLOSE all work inside one, measured on FILEDIR, which
## **  has opened the directory from a bank since 2026-09-07. A BANK statement
## **  is the only disqualifier.
## **
## ***********************************************************************
#IFNDEF SHIM.FUTILBANK.DEFS
#DEFINE SHIM.FUTILBANK.DEFS 1

## The bank the file modules run in. Not SHIM.GUIBANK -- that is the GUI's -- and
## not a scratch bank: BANKMGR.GET.FREE.BANK hands out the LOWEST free one, so 8
## sits above the library's block (4 the GUI, 5 and 6 the text, 7 the utilities)
## and leaves 1..3 to the run-time allocator. GP.BANKED takes a decimal constant
## and #DEFINE substitutes at translation time, so this and the BANK in each shim
## below cannot drift apart.
#DEFINE SHIM.FUTILBANK 8

## How deep the shims may nest. See FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH below.
#DEFINE FUTIL.SHIM.MAX 8

GOTO SHIM.FUTILBANK.MODULE.END

## ***********************************************************************
## **  FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH / FUTIL.SHIM.POP -- the caller's bank, kept and put back.
## **
## **  Every shim is PUSH, the body, POP. PUSH remembers which bank the caller
## **  had selected and selects this library's; POP puts the caller's back, so
## **  the instruction after the call is fetched from the right place.
## **
## **  A STACK PER SHIM FILE, and this is that file's. Pushes and pops pair up
## **  inside one file whatever the others are doing, so the front doors
## **  interleave correctly without sharing anything.
## **
## **  POP IS REACHED BY GOTO, NOT GOSUB. The shim's own GOSUB frame is still on
## **  the stack, so POP's RETURN is the shim's return.
## **
## **  SHIM.UTILBANK.INC.BL CARRIES THE REASONING in full -- why one holding
## **  variable is not enough, and why the capture is a blob rather than
## **  PEEK(0). Read it there; this is the same code under its own names.
## ***********************************************************************

## The array, once for the whole program. DIM cannot run twice, and no program
## should have to remember to call an init, so the first shim call does it.
##
## IT IS ABOVE THE BLOB AND NOT BELOW IT because GP.ASM resolves {FUTIL.SHIM.WAS%}
## against the variables the compiler has already met. Named first here, the
## blob can write it; named only inside the blob, the build stops with
## UNKNOWN VARIABLE IN {}.

FUTIL.SHIM.INIT:
    DIM FUTIL.SHIM.STK%(FUTIL.SHIM.MAX)
    FUTIL.SHIM.WAS% = 0
    FUTIL.SHIM.DIMMED = -1
    RETURN

FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH:
    IF FUTIL.SHIM.DIMMED = 0 THEN GOSUB FUTIL.SHIM.INIT
    #REM 1
    GP.ASM
    REM LDA $00
    REM STA {FUTIL.SHIM.WAS%}
    REM LDX #1
    REM LDA #0
    REM STA {FUTIL.SHIM.WAS%},X
    GP.ENDASM
    #REM 0
    FUTIL.SHIM.STK%(FUTIL.SHIM.SP) = FUTIL.SHIM.WAS%
    FUTIL.SHIM.SP = FUTIL.SHIM.SP + 1
    BANK SHIM.FUTILBANK
    RETURN

FUTIL.SHIM.POP:
    FUTIL.SHIM.SP = FUTIL.SHIM.SP - 1
    BANK FUTIL.SHIM.STK%(FUTIL.SHIM.SP)
    RETURN

## ---- FILEDIR ----
FILE.DIR.INIT:  GOSUB FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH : GOSUB FILE.DIR.INIT.BODY  : GOTO FUTIL.SHIM.POP
FILE.DIR.OPEN:  GOSUB FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH : GOSUB FILE.DIR.OPEN.BODY  : GOTO FUTIL.SHIM.POP
FILE.DIR.NEXT:  GOSUB FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH : GOSUB FILE.DIR.NEXT.BODY  : GOTO FUTIL.SHIM.POP

## ---- FILEIO ----
FILE.STATUS:    GOSUB FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH : GOSUB FILE.STATUS.BODY    : GOTO FUTIL.SHIM.POP
FILE.EXISTS:    GOSUB FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH : GOSUB FILE.EXISTS.BODY    : GOTO FUTIL.SHIM.POP
FILE.DELETE:    GOSUB FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH : GOSUB FILE.DELETE.BODY    : GOTO FUTIL.SHIM.POP
FILE.RENAME:    GOSUB FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH : GOSUB FILE.RENAME.BODY    : GOTO FUTIL.SHIM.POP
FILE.MKDIR:     GOSUB FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH : GOSUB FILE.MKDIR.BODY     : GOTO FUTIL.SHIM.POP
FILE.RMDIR:     GOSUB FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH : GOSUB FILE.RMDIR.BODY     : GOTO FUTIL.SHIM.POP
FILE.CHDIR:     GOSUB FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH : GOSUB FILE.CHDIR.BODY     : GOTO FUTIL.SHIM.POP
FILE.UP:        GOSUB FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH : GOSUB FILE.UP.BODY        : GOTO FUTIL.SHIM.POP
FILE.CURDIR:    GOSUB FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH : GOSUB FILE.CURDIR.BODY    : GOTO FUTIL.SHIM.POP
FILE.SAVEARRAY: GOSUB FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH : GOSUB FILE.SAVEARRAY.BODY : GOTO FUTIL.SHIM.POP
FILE.LOADARRAY: GOSUB FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH : GOSUB FILE.LOADARRAY.BODY : GOTO FUTIL.SHIM.POP

## FILE.SIZE is a VERB, not a shim. GP.DEFPROC compiles the call site into a jump
## to the body, and a call site in low memory jumping to $A000 does not select the
## bank first, so the declaration has to carry the bank change -- it is the one
## place the PUSH can go. Being a verb its name is a NAME and cannot also be a
## label, which is what removes GOSUB FILE.SIZE as a way to call it. FILE.OK is
## still set beside the count, which tells a real 0-block file from a missing one.
GP.DEFPROC FILE.SIZE, FILE.NAME$ RETURNS FILE.BLOCKS : GOSUB FUTIL.SHIM.PUSH : GOSUB FILE.SIZE.BODY
GOTO FUTIL.SHIM.POP

SHIM.FUTILBANK.MODULE.END:
#ENDIF
